        heading: 'Introduction: The Real Value Behind Reward Points',
        content: 'Banks advertise credit cards with flashy headlines: "Earn 10,000 bonus points!" or "5X points on weekend dining." But 10,000 points is not ₹10,000. In India, a single reward point can be worth anywhere from ₹0.10 to ₹1.00, depending entirely on the issuing bank, the card tier, and the redemption channel you select.\n\nUnderstanding the true rupee conversion rate of your points is essential to calculating whether a card\'s annual fee actually pays for itself or drains your finances.'
