        heading: '3. The Redemption Trap: Why Catalog Merchandise Is a Value Leak',
        content: 'The single biggest mistake credit card holders make is redeeming points for home appliances, luggage, or electronics from bank product catalogs.\n\n*Example:* A branded toaster costs ₹2,000 on Amazon. In the bank\'s rewards catalog, it is listed for 12,000 points (realized value = ₹0.16/point). If you redeemed those 12,000 points for travel or vouchers at ₹0.50, you would receive ₹6,000 in real value—wasting ₹4,000.\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Convert points exclusively to airline miles, hotel transfers, flight tickets, or high-liquidity shopping vouchers (Amazon/Flipkart).'
